{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790924022,"nonce":"ZGSEoGxmuKuxezTo6JM1M2KyPpg=","message":"**Added scope (orchestrator, per ADR 0055 §2 as amended 2026-10-02): a mapping never holds a secret.** A vendor key that must travel in the body (PagerDuty's `routing_key`) is stored as a sealed credential on the Connection (the `channel_credentials` pattern) and referenced from the mapping by name; oto resolves it at send time. Save-time validation refuses a mapping whose literal text looks like it embeds a credential where a reference is expected only if that can be done without false positives — otherwise the docs say it. **Done when (added):** a mapping referencing a named Connection secret renders it at send time; the mapping as stored and as exported to the catalog contains no secret; a reference to a missing secret fails validation.","files":null}]}